<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The genesis island ~ how one artifact gets built, and why the builder holds no doctrine

Every peer boots from one content-addressed genesis artifact, and the artifact carries the engine
that deserializes it. This room owns the BUILD of that artifact: what the runner reads off a disk,
what it declares about each blob, and what it refuses to decide.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/three-layers>>

!! Three layers, and the middle one touches no disk

# ''A reads.'' The node runner walks the TW5 core script, the vendored plugin JSONs and their build
attestations off the filesystem and assembles `GenesisInputs`.
# ''B builds.'' `buildGenesisDoc(inputs)` in mesh constructs the Automerge doc. Platform-neutral by
construction — it takes bytes and returns a document, so a browser vessel and a node vessel fold the
SAME artifact from the same inputs.
# ''C writes.'' The runner lands the artifact bytes, the CAS entries and the three region CIDs.

''The split is the portability.'' A build step that reached for `fs` inside layer B would bind the
artifact's shape to one host, and the artifact is the one thing every host must agree on exactly.

''What does NOT belong here.'' Corpus memes load at runtime through the bag store's recipe stack, and
oracle tiddlers (runtime DocUrls) write after `repo.import()` in `reconcileWellKnownTiddlers`. Neither
is genesis material: one is content the vessel carries, the other is state it discovers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-declaration>>

!! A blob's class is DECLARED at the mint, never read off its path

Each vendored file arrives as one of three classes, and `collectPlugins` decides which by READING it:

* ''grammar'' — the required memetic-wikitext plugin, matched by its own URI. One file, and the whole
of kāhuli's fast ratchet.
* ''plugin'' — a file whose JSON envelope declares a `title`. This operator's own collection.
* ''base'' — the default, and what an envelope-less tiddler array or an unparseable file stands as.
The `lararium-boot-shadows` seed lives here, beside the lares/lararium bags.

''The default is base, and that is the safe direction.'' A file that declares nothing gets the class
that ratchets nothing; only a file that SAYS it is a plugin becomes one. An unparseable blob takes the
same road rather than failing the build, because it declared nothing either.

''The class rides INTO the descriptor,'' so verification classifies exactly as the mint did. A gate
that re-derived the class from a path would be a second reader, free to disagree with the first — the
[[carrier gradient|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/carrier-gradient]] lesson, one layer down.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/regions>>

!! Three regions, two ratchets

The build prints and lands three CIDs, and they are not three tiers of one thing:

|!Region |!What it folds |!What advancing it means |
|`engineCid` |the TW5 core — the hearth true-name |the SLOW ratchet; it re-binds membership mesh-wide and rides inside every signed device-delegation preimage |
|`grammarCid` |the required grammar ALONE |kāhuli's FAST ratchet — an overturn the mesh takes together |
|`pluginsCid` |this operator's own collection |a REGION, never a kāhuli tier — any operator offers their own, and plugin drift is not grammar drift |

''The engine's preimage is not a region fold.'' `computeEngineCid` takes `(version, sha)` and excludes
the version label deliberately; the other two fold their entries under their OWN domain literal. Three
hand-written folds read like an inconsistency and are the separation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/determinism>>

!! The actor seed makes two builds the same build

`actorSeed = sha256hex(sorted content hashes of every walked input)`, so two builds from identical
source produce an identical `island.sha256`. Automerge would otherwise stamp a fresh actor per build
and two byte-identical corpora would fold to two different artifacts — which would make the artifact
useless as a name.

''An attestation that disagrees with its blob ABORTS the build.'' A plugin whose recorded
`pluginJsonSha256` misses the bytes on disk throws rather than vendoring; a half-true genesis is worse
than none, because every vessel downstream would carry the lie by hash.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

